course: dictionary
lesson: 9902
title: Words that describe people
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A word that describes a person tells us what they are like. Talkative is an adjective: it describes someone who talks a lot, often in a friendly, chatty way. You can say a talkative child, very talkative, or in a talkative mood.
explain: Look at this sentence: «The car's owners are hungry, talkative, and gay.» The words are listed together, so they all describe the owners. Talkative tells us the owners chat a lot. Gay is an old word here that means cheerful, so check a dictionary if you meet it in other books.
explain: Teachers sometimes write that a pupil is talkative in school reports. It can be a gentle way of saying a pupil chats too much in class. Read the words around it to be sure, just as you would with any new word.
fact: Talkative means talking a lot, often in a friendly and chatty way.
fact: Talkative is an adjective, so it can change: talkative, more talkative, most talkative.
fact: Chatty is a close synonym: a chatty friend is a talkative friend.
fact: Phrases such as «a talkative child», «very talkative» and «in a talkative mood» show how the word is used.
fact: In a story, a talkative character might be a chatty parrot or a friend who never stops talking.
exercise: «Mia is very talkative, and she tells everyone about her holiday.» What does talkative mean here? | Very quiet | *Talks a lot | Ran very fast | Likes to sleep
exercise: Which word means about the same as talkative? | Silent | *Chatty | Tall | Angry
exercise: Find the word that tells us what the girl is like: «The talkative girl told us all about her week.» | girl | told | *talkative | week
test: «In a talkative mood, Sam told the whole class about his dog.» What does talkative mean? | *Chatting a lot | Quiet and shy | Sleepy and yawning | Angry with everyone
test: Which form of talkative means the most talkative? | *most talkative | talkatively | talkativer | more talker
exam: «Our teacher said my cousin is talkative, but she is also kind.» What does talkative tell us about the cousin? | She is good at maths | *She talks a lot and is chatty | She never speaks at all | She is very tired
